Label the two sides of the equation: \[\begin{aligned}
\text{left}\;\;&\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix}, \\
\text{right}\;\;&\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} + s \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}. \end{aligned}\end{think}
<answer>By equation (2), we have \[ \begin{aligned} 1+7t&=-2s, \\ -1-5t&=3s. \end{aligned} \]By (1) twice, (2) once, we have $9s=3$ and $9s=-16$ so $s=\frac13$ ... By (1) once and (2) three times, we have $28\frac13 t=-5$ and $-32\frac13 t=-12$ so $t=-\frac{1}{14}$ ... Therefore, $(t,s)=\boxed{\left(-\frac{1}{14},\frac{1}{3}\right)}.$</answer>

